 ## Status & roadmap
 
-- **Admin API integration is delivered** ([#41543](https://github.com/PrestaShop/PrestaShop/issues/41543)) — see *Admin API integration* above. Defining extra properties *through* the API (CRUD on the registry itself) is still open [#41542](https://github.com/PrestaShop/PrestaShop/issues/41542). The BO definition management CQRS layer added by this branch is separate from the Admin API bridge.
+- **Admin API integration is delivered** ([#41543](https://github.com/PrestaShop/PrestaShop/issues/41543)) — see *Admin API integration* above. Defining extra properties *through* the API (CRUD + list on the registry itself, [#41542](https://github.com/PrestaShop/PrestaShop/issues/41542)) lives in `ps_apiresources` (`/extra-property-definitions`, resources under `src/ApiPlatform/Resources/ExtraPropertyDefinition/`, gated `minVersion 9.2.0`): it wraps the BO definition management CQRS layer as-is — constraints as the DSL string, enums as their string value, `defaultValue` typed, `shopIds` for the shop association — and its tests (`ExtraPropertyDefinitionEndpointTest`, `ExtraPropertyValuesEndpointTest`, `ExtraPropertyMultiShopEndpointTest`) cover the definition contract plus the runtime effect of API-created definitions on the real module endpoints. The CQRS error matrix (refused DSL, registry refusals) is owned by the core Behat suite, so the API tests assert one error per HTTP mapping only.
 - **Module uninstall cleanup is not automatic** — modules must call `unregisterExtraProperty($definition, dropData: true)` themselves.
 - Multishop handling [#41568] is implemented — see the *ShopConstraint semantics* bullet above (fan-out writes, representative-shop reads, schema-derived `isMultiShop()` detection). Definition-level shop association (restricting a definition to a list of shops) is implemented too — see the *definition-level shop association* bullet; the companion autoupgrade PR adds `extra_property_definition_shop` to `upgrade/sql/9.2.0.sql`.
 - Cart entity [#41424] is supported (COMMON scope only — no `cart_lang`/`cart_shop` base table, the cart's `id_lang`/`id_shop` being plain columns; LANG/SHOP registrations are cleanly rejected). The presented cart (`CartLazyArray`, the `$cart` Smarty global) exposes values under `extra_properties` (snake_case — `extraProperties` is Admin-API-JSON-only spelling), and `CartFilter` whitelists the key so the JS `prestashop.cart` object carries it. Cart values die with the cart at checkout: modules needing post-order visibility copy them onto the order at `actionValidateOrder` (demoextrafield demonstrates the pattern).
